    getChunkNaturalTreeCandidates.
  - 07f8282 "perf(worldgen): solve modern terrain columns lazily with a
    banded surface search" (biomenoise.c only): 1.18+ columns solve
    density cells on demand from the top and start the surface search a
    fixed band below the noise-free density-zero crossing; pre-1.18
    generators keep their original path.
  - feat/gpu-opencl (02b70a1..1a3386c, ten commits) "OpenCL GPU executor
    for 1.18+ Overworld surface biomes and terrain overview heights":
    gpu.c/gpu.h/gpu_cl_kernels.h + opencl_host.c/h behind the compile-time
    gate CUBIOMES_ENABLE_GPU, which turns mapOverworldSurfaceBiome /
    mapOverworldTerrainHeight into transparent try-GPU-then-CPU dispatches.
    The host dlopens the platform OpenCL loader (no link-time dependency);
    absence degrades silently to the CPU path. GPU outputs are a float
    approximation of the double CPU reference, gated by the drift-budget
    harness (make gpu-test in the submodule: per-distance-bucket biome-flip
    and height/climate budgets plus exact query-shape-invariance and
    mode-handling checks). Batched z-stride entries
    (gpuMapOverworldSurfaceBiomeRows / gpuMapOverworldTerrainHeightRows)
    fold streamed overview-row sets into one dispatch. Default mode is
    env-driven (CUBIOMES_GPU, auto); gpuSetMode() overrides.
  - Nether fossils: upstream 32f6624 now ships its own terrain-validated
    fossil model, so the fork keeps only what upstream lacks - the
    getFeaturePos routing in getStructurePos (upstream leaves fossils
    unplaced; the shim's structure catalog depends on the anchor-chunk
    contract) and the versioned anchor-biome rule in isViableStructurePos.
  - StructureType enum order follows upstream (Nether_Fossil=20,
    Abandoned_Camp=26, Stronghold=27); StructureIndex in the parent repo
    pins the same ordinals.

